# No Agent Signatures in User-Facing Output

The `fqc-arr` agent (and any future agent in this repo) must never embed its own name, brand, sub-agent name, or "auto-generated by …" tag in any output a human reads on Jira, Slack, GitHub, or in a generated file's docstring.

## What counts as user-facing output

- Jira comments (ADF body posted via REST API)
- Slack messages (heartbeats, banners, role-result updates, DMs)
- PR titles, PR bodies, commit messages, review comments
- Docstrings / headers of files the agent generates and writes to disk (tests, fixtures, LLM prompt scratch files)

## Banned patterns (in user-facing output)

- `Posted by FQC-ARR …`
- `Authored by Finance ARR Quarter Close (FQC-ARR) supervisor for …`
- `Auto-created by the FQC-ARR debugger sub-agent for …`
- `Generated by …`, `Sent by …`, `Created automatically by …`
- `FQC-ARR debugger: <title>`, `FQC-ARR debugger findings for …`
- `:rocket: *Finance ARR Quarter Close (FQC-ARR) started*` (Slack banner branding)
- Any other "this comment / PR / message came from the agent" tagline

## Allowed (internal-only)

- Module docstrings, README files, `.cursor/rules/`, `.cursor/skills/`
- Internal Python constants (`SUPERVISOR_DISPLAY_NAME`, `SUPERVISOR_SHORT_CODE`) as long as they are not interpolated into user-facing output
- LLM system prompts the agent sends to its own subagents (these are not read by humans)
- Local terminal output from the CLI (the user is already aware they ran the command)
- The thinking-log file (`runs/thinking/*.md`) — internal trace, not posted anywhere
- Slack channel/bot display name set at the workspace level (Slack metadata, not message text)

## How to write user-facing copy

Lead with the substance. The Jira ticket key, model name, PR number, or quarter date is the identifier humans care about — not the agent's name.

```python
# BAD - signature in Jira ADF title
title = f"FQC-ARR debugger: root cause + reproducible fix for {ticket_key}"

# GOOD - identifier first, no agent self-reference
title = f"Root cause + reproducible fix for {ticket_key}"
```

```python
# BAD - signature footer in PR body
return f"""...
_Authored by Finance ARR Quarter Close (FQC-ARR) supervisor for {ticket_key}._
"""

# GOOD - body ends with the last useful section, no footer
return f"""...
## Reviewer checklist
- [ ] ...
"""
```

```python
# BAD - branded Slack banner
head = f":rocket: *{self.display_name} started*"

# GOOD - status verb + the identifier the human asked about
head = ":rocket: *Started*"
if self.label:
    head += f" - `{self.label}`"  # e.g. "EDAEM-3772"
```

## When in doubt

If a human will read it on a system outside this terminal, strip the agent's identity. Keep the substance (root cause, fix, test results, PR diff, reviewer asks) front and center.
